BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 515.95 Td (Production compilers such as GCC and LLVM/Clang run a fixed, preset order of optimization passes inside levels) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 503.95 Td (like -O1, -O2 and -O3. Compiler transformations are non-commutative, so no single ordering suits every) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 491.95 Td (program, and with N passes there are N! possible orderings. Each pass is designed assuming a local benefit,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 479.95 Td (yet in practice an apparently beneficial pass can degrade the IR and yield worse machine code. Three typical) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 467.95 Td (causes are register-pressure explosion \(aggressive CSE or LICM extends live ranges and forces memory spills\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 455.95 Td (code bloat and instruction-cache thrashing \(aggressive inlining and unrolling\), and phase destabilization \(an) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 443.95 Td (early pass destroys the canonical patterns that later passes need\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 427.95 Td (The gap is that passes run speculatively and irreversibly. Existing compilers and autotuners search for good) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 415.95 Td (orderings offline or at flag level, but none measure the IR between passes, and none can atomically undo a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 403.95 Td (harmful pass. This project addresses the need for a compiler that treats every optimization pass as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 391.95 Td (transaction: measure it, keep it if it helps, and roll it back if it hurts.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.50 Tf 45.00 369.95 Td (Objectives \(Minimum 3\)) Tj ET
