BT /F2 10.50 Tf 45.00 569.50 Td (Research gaps and project motivation) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 556.50 Td (The surveyed work falls into three groups. Search-based approaches \(iterative compilation, genetic algorithms,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 545.00 Td (OpenTuner\) and learning-based approaches \(Milepost, MiCOMP, AutoPhase\) look for a good pass ordering or flag set,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 533.50 Td (but they work offline or at macro-flag level and depend on expensive measurement on target hardware. Formal work) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 522.00 Td (on transformation interactions and on translation validation shows that passes can undermine each other and can) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 510.50 Td (even be wrong, yet it offers no way to recover at compile time, and the register-allocation literature only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 499.00 Td (reveals spills after the fact. Autotuning surveys explicitly name optimization degradation as an unsolved problem) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 487.50 Td (and ask for self-stabilizing compilers. None of these systems measures the IR between passes or reverts a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 476.00 Td (harmful pass. This motivates OptiGuard, which scores each IR state in situ and treats every pass as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 45.00 464.50 Td (commit-or-rollback transaction.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.00 Tf 45.00 441.00 Td (Novelty - 2 M) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 45.00 428.00 Td (OptiGuard differs from the literature reviewed in the following ways:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 50.00 416.00 Td (*) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 60.00 416.00 Td (Transactional compilation model:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 220.80 416.00 Td (* Transactional compilation model: database-style atomicity and consistency are applied to phase ordering, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 404.50 Td (every pass is a speculative transaction that is either committed or rolled back. Existing pipelines are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 393.00 Td (sequential and irreversible.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 50.00 379.50 Td (*) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 60.00 379.50 Td (In-situ cost evaluation J\(IR\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 211.00 379.50 Td (* In-situ cost evaluation J\(IR\): passes are scored directly on the TAC using instruction count, live intervals) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 368.00 Td (and operator-weighted ALU cycles, which removes the target-hardware re-execution that GA and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 356.50 Td (iterative-compilation approaches need.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 50.00 343.00 Td (*) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 60.00 343.00 Td (Micro-pass granularity with atomic rollback:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 279.60 343.00 Td (* Micro-pass granularity with atomic rollback: degradation is detected and reverted at the level of a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 331.50 Td (pass, so the culprit is isolated. Prior work discards or merely penalizes an entire sequence.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 50.00 318.00 Td (*) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.20 Tf 60.00 318.00 Td (Tabu-driven adaptive scheduling:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 220.80 318.00 Td (* Tabu-driven adaptive scheduling: a degrading pass is recorded in a tabu list for that IR state, which prevents) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 60.00 306.50 Td (cyclic rollbacks and steers the scheduler toward alternative passes chosen from IR features.) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.20 Tf 45.00 289.00 Td (Formal novelty statement: unlike existing compiler optimization pipelines that apply transformations sequentially) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.20 Tf 45.00 277.50 Td (and irreversibly regardless of intermediate code deterioration, OptiGuard introduces a fail-safe, transactional) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.20 Tf 45.00 266.00 Td (compiler architecture that combines IR feature) Tj ET
